<title>DUBAI: Total to buy 30-60,000 bpd of Iraq oil under plan.</title>
<headline>Total to buy 30-60,000 bpd of Iraq oil under plan.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Total SA will buy 30,000-60,000 barrels per day of Iraqi crude under the United Nations-approved humanitarian oil sales plan, the London-based Arabic daily al-Hayat reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Al-Hayat quoted Total's director of Middle East affairs Christophe Dumarjorie in Paris as saying the purchases would be made once the oil-for-food deal came into effect.</p>
<p>U.N. Secretary General Boutros Boutros-Ghali delayed implementing the deal after Iraqi forces attacked Kurdish rebels in northern Iraq on August 31.</p>
<p>Iraq urged the U.N. on Sunday to implement the deal -- which allows Baghdad to sell $2 billion of its oil over six months in exchange for food and other humanitarian supplies -- as soon as possible.</p>
<p>-- Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255</p>
